 body:'Before the plaques and the packed rooms, there was a bedroom, a borrowed laptop and a notebook full of verses nobody had heard yet. Every night after work he recorded, mixed and posted, building a sound one song at a time.\n\nThe first shows were small: a few friends, a few strangers, a sound system that cut out twice. But the strangers came back, and they brought people with them. By the end of the year the venue had to turn fans away at the door.\n\nWhat changed was not luck. It was a plan: drop music every Friday, answer every message, show up to every open mic in the city, and never wait for a label to say yes.\n\nQ: How did it start?\nA: In my bedroom with a laptop and a cheap mic. I just kept going.\n\nQ: What is next?\nA: A full project this spring and a tour in every city that showed love.\n\nDonec ullamcorper nulla non metus auctor fringilla. Maecenas faucibus mollis interdum. Cras mattis consectetur purus sit amet fermentum.\n\nNullam quis risus eget urna mollis ornare vel eu leo. Vivamus sagittis lacus vel augue laoreet rutrum faucibus dolor auctor.\n\nQ: How did it start?\nA: In my bedroom with a laptop.',
